<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottonian Handfeste</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1311</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Ottonische Handfeste</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ottonian Handfeste was a charter issued in 1311 by Duke Otto III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-bavaria">Lower Bavaria</a> in return for a special tax to pay his debts. It sold the lower jurisdiction over their own people to the nobles, clergy and towns of Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>. It is regarded as the foundation of the Bavarian estates, whose consent to taxation became a lasting check on ducal power.</p></div>
